Q: Add nullability check for out variable that isn&#39;t properly annotated A: <p>I came up with an extension method that could invoke the out function, and applies the attribute. Usage isn't too bad.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>// need to create delegate for supported signatures
public delegate bool TryFunc&lt;TIn, TOut&gt;(TIn input, out TOut? output);
static class Extensions
{
    // applies to all types, could be targeted
    public static bool Try&lt;TIn, TOut&gt;(this object source, TryFunc&lt;TIn, TOut&gt; tryFunc, TIn input, [NotNullWhen(true)] out TOut output)
    {
        return Try(tryFunc, input, out output);
    }

    public static bool Try&lt;TIn, TOut&gt;(TryFunc&lt;TIn, TOut&gt; tryFunc, TIn input, [NotNullWhen(true)] out TOut output)
    {
        return tryFunc(input, out output!);
    }
}

// usage
if (!obj.Try(obj.TryGetProperty, &quot;b&quot;, out string? b)) // need explicit types
{
    ...
}

// or 

using static Extensions;
if (!Try(obj.TryGetProperty, &quot;b&quot;, out string? b))
{
    ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now, the following will hold:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>if (!obj.TryGetProperty(&quot;a&quot;, out var a))
    return;
if (!obj.Try(obj.TryGetProperty, &quot;b&quot;, out string? b))
    return;
if (!Try(obj.TryGetProperty, &quot;c&quot;, out string? c))
    return;
// a may or may not be null
// b is not null
// c is not null
</code></pre>
<p>Only problem is that this is limited to the basic signature: <code>bool Function(TIn input, out TOut? output);</code> Would need to add other delegates/overloads for other signatures.</p>
